clearcote: system-ui must resolve, and must resolve to the persona's system font.

Measured: `system-ui` rendered at 841.47 in the container -- byte-identical to an unresolvable
family name, i.e. it did not resolve AT ALL. On Windows it is 895.86, the same width as Segoe UI
(genuine Chrome 151 and our Windows build agree exactly). A page comparing the generic against the
concrete family needs no reference data, and the control for "unresolved" is any garbage string.

Root cause: on Linux FontCache::SystemFontFamily() returns whatever the browser pushed through
renderer preferences (web_view_impl.cc). In a bare container nothing sets it, so the static
AtomicString stays EMPTY and system-ui has nothing to resolve to.

A fontconfig <alias> does NOT fix this -- tried and measured, no effect -- because Blink substitutes
this value before fontconfig is consulted and never asks for a family named "system-ui". The fix has
to live here.

Answers "Segoe UI", which the bundled fonts.conf already maps to the Selawik clone, and which
measures correctly in the container today, so the target is known good rather than hoped for. Gated:
a Linux persona keeps the stock pref-driven value.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/linux/font_cache_linux.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/linux/font_cache_linux.cc
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/simple_font_data.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/font_fallback_linux.h"
+#include "build/build_config.h"
+#include "components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h"
 
 namespace blink {
 
@@ -41,6 +43,22 @@
 
 // static
 const AtomicString& FontCache::SystemFontFamily() {
+  // clearcote(r16): a Windows persona must resolve system-ui to its system font. On Linux this
+  // value comes from renderer preferences (web_view_impl.cc), which nothing sets in a bare
+  // container -- so it stays EMPTY and CSS system-ui resolves to nothing. Measured: system-ui
+  // rendered at exactly the width of an unresolvable family, while a Windows host renders it at
+  // the width of Segoe UI. That is readable with two measureText calls and no reference data.
+  //
+  // Segoe UI is the correct answer for a Windows persona and is already mapped to the bundled
+  // Selawik clone by fonts.conf, where it measures correctly today. A fontconfig alias for
+  // "system-ui" does NOT work (measured): Blink substitutes this value before fontconfig is
+  // consulted, so the fix has to live here.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  if (ungoogled::GetPersonaPlatform() == ungoogled::PersonaPlatform::kWindows) {
+    DEFINE_THREAD_SAFE_STATIC_LOCAL(AtomicString, cc_segoe, ("Segoe UI"));
+    return cc_segoe;
+  }
+#endif
   return MutableSystemFontFamily();
 }
 
